WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.870
it's Michelle from Lab Muffin Beauty
science and I am a massive sunscreen

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:09.929
nerd since I talk about sunscreens all
the time

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:14.099
I've been asked by a lot of people to
review my favorite sunscreens so today

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.670
I'm going to be talking about my six
favorites from my sunscreen spreadsheet

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:22.230
which I've given a 5 plus rating in the
future I hope there'll be more sunscreens

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.650
joining this group if you like this sort
of video give it a thumbs up subscribe

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.099
to my channel and click the notification
bell so you don't miss any videos

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.520
everyone looks for different things in
the sunscreen my skin is not the same as

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.239
your skin so don't just go out and buy
these sunscreens and expect them to work

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:45.809
just as well for you as they did for me
if you want to work out what your skin

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:49.230
type and concerns are or if you want
more info on choosing and using a

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:53.190
sunscreen you can check out my book the
lab muffin guide to basic skincare so

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:57.690
here's what I look for in a sunscreen I
look for high UVA protection and that's

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.770
because I'm really really prone to
hyperpigmentation which is when you get

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.090
sunspots and when you get brown marks
after acne that don't fade for ages

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:10.500
and ages I have another video on this
topic so for high UVA protection I look

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.299
for a PA or PPD rating or I look for the
words broad spectrum from a place that

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:19.890
has stricter guidelines like Australia I
also look for the newer UVA filters all

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.340
of the sunscreens I'm talking about
today have these these are things like

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:29.400
Tinosorbs S and M, Uvinul A Plus and
Meroxyl SX and XL if you want to know more

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.060
about sunscreen ingredients there's a
free downloadable sample from the lab muffin

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.270
guide to basic skincare that goes
through some of the different UV filters

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.560
another really important factor for me
is lack of a white cast this is when you

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:45.030
apply your sunscreen and you see like a
sort of white film over your face I've

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:49.979
had this with every single inorganic or
mineral sunscreen I've tried so all of

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.329
the ones on this list are chemical or
organic my skin is actually still on the

00:01:54.329 --> 00:01:58.170
pretty pale side it's NC 20 but I can
still notice this white cast when I

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:01.710
apply the full amount that I meant to I've
done a video in the past about the

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.829
differences between chemical and
physical sunscreens but for me

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:09.000
personally white cast has been the deal
breaker I have included one mineral

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.020
sunscreen in the honorable mentions at
the end of this

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:16.130
so if you prefer those sorts of
sunscreens stay tuned another really

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.450
important consideration for me is how
easy it is to apply the sunscreen I like

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.720
to be able to spread the sunscreen on
and not have to work it into my skin too

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.310
much and I really hate it when it pills
or balls up because I know that that's

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:32.240
protection that's just leaving my skin
whether or not a sunscreen pills or

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.870
balls up on you really depends on your
skin type so my skin is oily combination

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.160
and these ones have been fine for me I
like to apply my sunscreen really close

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.450
to my eyes because that's where all the
wrinkles are coming my eyes are pretty

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:48.050
resilient because I've been wearing
contact lenses for years but they do

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.380
still water with some sunscreens so this
is pretty important for me as well

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.940
obviously clogged pores are evil and my
skin really likes to clog up with

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:00.290
sunscreens I don't know why all of the
sunscreens I've been trying I've been

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.310
trying for at least two weeks and most
of them do clog my pores at some point

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:09.470
these six have not so onto the
sunscreens these six are my favorite so

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:13.640
far all of them are Asian or Australian
and I promise you that's not just

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.050
because they're like me and I love me I
haven't got any US sunscreens on there

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.370
because in the US the new UVA filters
haven't been approved yet so I don't

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:26.570
really like the chance of me getting a
high UVA protection factor sunscreen

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:30.200
there I also haven't got any European
sunscreens on the list and I think

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.010
that's because even though they do have
the newer UVA filters their sunscreens

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:37.220
tend to be a lot more heavy and I think
that's because they have a dry climate

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.600
and people tend to have dry skin I have
very oily skin and I live in Australia

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.710
so the texture just doesn't really work
for me so far the first sunscreen is

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:49.280
canmake's mermaid skin gel UV I've
decided to start with the Asian

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.370
sunscreens because they're a bit easier
for people to find and buy than

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:57.050
Australian sunscreens this is a really
really light textured sunscreen one of

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.770
the lightest sunscreens I've ever tried
and it's so light that sometimes I

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.060
wonder how sweat resistant it is it
sinks in really easily it works really

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.720
well under makeup and there's no alcohol
in it which is good if you're prone to

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.440
dehydrated skin it's unscented and
there's also no white cast which is

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.620
awesome I was actually surprised by the
fact that wasn't white cast because it

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:20.000
does contain some inorganic sunscreens
as well so this is a combo inorganic

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.610
and chemical sunscreen there are five
sunscreen actives in this they're

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:29.310
zinc oxide titanium dioxide uvinul a
plus tinosorb s and octinoxate I

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.520
don't really like titanium dioxide in
sunscreens because it tends to give you

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.150
white cast and it's also quite photo
reactive which means it makes other

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:40.229
things react in terms of skincare
ingredients in sunscreens I don't really

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:43.530
tend to care that much about them
because that's not what I'm using

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:47.280
sunscreen for they are a nice bonus but
I wouldn't go out of my way to choose

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.819
a sunscreen that has them the only
exception here is niacinamide which has

00:04:50.819 --> 00:04:54.389
been found to boost the immune system so
it's good for preventing certain types

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.469
of skin cancer this does have plant
extracts which are antioxidant but the

00:04:58.469 --> 00:05:02.129
main thing I like this sunscreen for is
it's incredibly light texture which is

00:05:02.129 --> 00:05:06.780
really comfortable and a really nice
beginner sunscreen if you haven't been

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.139
wearing daily sunscreen before because
of the texture the next sunscreen is

00:05:10.139 --> 00:05:15.330
Klairs Soft Airy UV Essence this is also
a really light water-based sunscreen

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:19.469
it's a little bit heavier than the
canmake one but it's still very very light

00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:23.580
again it's alcohol free which is great
if your skin is dehydration prone it has

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.479
a really light scent as well there's two
sunscreen ingredients in this there's

00:05:27.479 --> 00:05:31.710
uvinul a plus which protects against
UVA and octyl triazone which protects

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:35.039
against UVB there's been some
speculation that these two sunscreen

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:38.969
filters aren't enough to give you
protection against the full range of UV

00:05:38.969 --> 00:05:43.199
wavelengths I think this comes from one
of two places firstly there's a lot of

00:05:43.199 --> 00:05:47.879
incorrect info online about what
uvinul a plus does it does protect

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:53.250
against UVA1 and in fact BASF who
sell it sell it specifically as a UVA1

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.150
filter the other place where I think
this comes from is just people not quite

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:00.810
understanding how to read a UV
absorption graph the amount of UV

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.949
absorption depends on concentration as
well as the formula so the lines on the

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:08.370
graph will go up and down and if there's
an overlapping section you actually have

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:12.089
to take the two and add them together
to get an approximation of the

00:06:12.089 --> 00:06:15.930
absorbance whenever you have theoretical
speculation versus actual empirical

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.569
evidence like an SPF test or a PA rating
then the actual test will always overrule

00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:25.919
any theoretical speculation about what
the product can do as I said before you

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:29.430
can't predict how a recipe will taste if
you just look at the ingredients list

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:33.690
and I think this is what people are
doing in this case it's got SPF 50+

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:37.860
and PA++++ so it's maxed out
with both this has no white cast which

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:41.310
is not very surprising since it doesn't
have any inorganic filters it's got a

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:44.130
few skincare ingredients as well it's
got sea buckthorn oil which has

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.910
antioxidants it's also got allantoin and
beta glucan which are really good

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:53.040
moisturisers and niacinamide which is a
really good all-rounder ingredient I'm

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.700
reviewing both of these together because
they're incredibly similar sunscreens

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:00.930
these are the purito centella green
level safe sun &amp; centella green level

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:05.280
unscented sun this is basically just the
unscented version of this one these two

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.540
have the same sunscreen ingredients as
the class and in terms of texture these

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.010
are the next step up after class they're
a little bit heavier but they're still

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:18.210
really really light and really
comfortable I'd say they're sort of like

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:21.840
a light lotion I do like the fact that
the texture is a little bit heavier

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.650
because it feels like it will last for a
little bit longer on your skin in hot

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:29.250
weather even though it hasn't been
properly tested with a water resistance

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.140
rating these glide on really smoothly
and it's really easy to apply a large

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:37.770
amount on your skin which is important
because if you don't apply enough you

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.460
won't get full protection I've also
found that sometimes lighter sunscreens

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:45.060
tend to feel like they're just gliding
around on your face and they're not

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.940
really sinking in and so you're just
moving it around and you can't add any

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.090
more but that's not the case with these
ones or the previous ones that I talked

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:54.420
about either they didn't sting my eyes
and they make a really good makeup base

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:58.530
in terms of extra skin care ingredients
they have obviously centella extract

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.940
which is the name of the line
there's also niacinamide as well as

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.750
hyaluronic acid and glycerin which are
really good humectant moisturisers the

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.080
difference between the two obviously
there's the scent which I've talked

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.470
about before the scent in this comes
from lavender oil as well as Roman

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.980
chamomile so if you're allergic to
either of those then you should go for

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:20.640
the unscented the other benefit of the
unscented version is that it's got extra

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.630
centilla extracts as well I've talked
about this sunscreen a lot before it is

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:28.830
the ultraceuticals daily moisturiser
SPF 30 this has been my favorite

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:33.330
sunscreen for a really long time and I
think a lot of it is just I'm really

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.780
nostalgic because this is the first
sunscreen that didn't give me clogged

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.900
pores after I used it for a long time
there are three versions of this

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:43.410
sunscreen there's the mattifying which
is this one there's a hydrating version

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:48.030
and there's an SPF 50 plus version as
well in terms of the texture the SPF 50

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:50.930
plus is a little
heavier and the hydrating is a bit stickier

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:54.920
so I tend to use all three because
the textures aren't that dissimilar but

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.390
I tend to use the hydrating and the SPF
50 plus more in winter I also really

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.210
like the convenient pump top which
apart from being convenient which is

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:06.200
great because I'm lazy it's also really
good for making sure that you're not

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:10.940
using less and less sunscreen over time
the downside is that it is quite pricey

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:15.800
and for ultraceuticals I don't mind
paying more as much because I know that

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:20.450
they invest a lot of money into research
and clinical trials and that makes me

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:24.140
feel better than if I'm buying a luxury
product from a brand that invests all of

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.350
its money back into marketing another
thing I really like about the ultraceuticals

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.130
sunscreen is that you can get a
full ingredients listing as well as the

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.940
active ingredients and their percentages
in Australia sunscreens are classified

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.940
as medications which means that they
don't need to show all the inactive

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:41.990
ingredients I really appreciate that
ultraceuticals have chosen to show

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:45.710
them anyway because I think it makes
it much easier if you are a somewhat

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:50.000
nerdy consumer in terms of actives it's
got octinoxate avobenzone ensulizole

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.350
and tinosorb s the next
sunscreen on my list is ultra violette 

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:58.310
supreme screen and this is another brand
that's chosen to show the full

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:03.050
ingredients list it's also got a
convenient pump top and the packaging in

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:07.550
general is just really nice and fancy
ultra violette also make it really clear

00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:11.150
how much sunscreen you should be
applying to your skin which I appreciate

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:15.410
because there's just not that much
consumer education about this from most

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:19.610
sunscreen brands ultra violette so far have
three sunscreens and the other two

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.780
didn't really work for my skin I do know
that lots of other people have found

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:27.170
that they work so I think it is more of
a skin type issue than a product issue

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:31.580
but this is the one for me this is a
lightweight sunscreen that feels like it

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:36.410
sinks in pretty quickly and it leaves a
silky primer finish which makes a really

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.870
good makeup base it doesn't pill up or
ball at all

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:43.790
it has a light scent the three sunscreen
ingredients in it are tinosorb s and M

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:47.780
as well as octinoxate I'm a bit
cautious about tinosorb M because it's

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.460
an organic sunscreen but it does tend to
give a bit of white cast because it has

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:58.430
a physical action like it reflects and
scatters some light for this sunscreen I

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:02.010
didn't have any issues with white cast
supreme screen is designed to be

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:05.520
really hydrating so it's got lots of
humectants it's got glycerin butylene

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:09.270
glycol and saccharide
isomerate there is alcohol near the top

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:12.450
of the ingredients list but it's still
really hydrating and I think it's

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:17.010
because the humectants and the sunscreen
overpower the alcohol's dehydrating

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:21.420
effect overall my skin just felt really
hydrated when using it it also has some

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:24.990
antioxidants it's got kakadu plum
extract and it's got l-carnosine as

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:29.160
well the downside to the sunscreen is
the price per mL it's actually more

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.270
expensive than the ultraceuticals but
it does come in a smaller pack which

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.850
means that upfront the cost is a bit
lower

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:41.190
the final sunscreen on my list is
azclear's day moisturizer SPF 30 this is

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:46.020
made by ego pharmaceuticals who also
make sunsense and QV and it's part of

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:50.130
their azclear range which is a range of
products designed to work with an

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:54.000
azelaic acid treatment the reason I'm so
excited about the sunscreen is that it's

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:59.340
really really light and it's also really
really budget-friendly it is light but

00:11:59.340 --> 00:12:03.660
it is really humectant heavy so it's
really hydrating and it does tend to dry

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:08.070
down a little bit on the sticky and dewy
side I've only tried it in winter so far

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:13.740
so it's been fine but I do wonder how it
will hold up on my skin in summer cos

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:17.580
I'm quite oily I think if your skin is
drier then it will be much better for

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:23.070
you it does only have SPF 30 but it's
easy to apply a lot and if you can apply

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:27.480
a lot of an SPF 30 it still ends up
probably being better than applying a

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:32.400
tiny bit of an SPF 50 plus the active
ingredients in this octinoxate tinosorb

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:36.510
s and uvinul a plus this does work
well under makeup even though it doesn't

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:40.470
really have that primer finish it's more
of like a moisturiser finish and one of

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:43.620
the problems I've had with ego
sunscreens in the past is that some of

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.800
them tend to ball up when you're
applying makeup it hasn't been a

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.580
problem at all with this I have some
honorable mentions which have missed out

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:54.990
on being one of my Holy Grail sunscreens
because of one small issue firstly

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:59.730
there's the purito comfy water sunblock
which is purito's inorganic sunscreen

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:05.610
the reason this didn't make it into my
top is because it does give a tiny white

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.420
cast it has the least white cast of any
inorganic sunscreen I've ever tried it

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:13.970
feels really light but it has enough
white cast that when I put on my foundation

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:17.389
it looks like it's not quite the right
colour so that is still a deal-breaker

00:13:17.389 --> 00:13:22.209
for me but if you're lighter if it's not
such a big deal for you then this is a

00:13:22.209 --> 00:13:26.689
really low white cast inorganic
sunscreen there's also the natio

00:13:26.689 --> 00:13:30.439
daily defense moisturizer this is the
one that I tend to recommend to friends

00:13:30.439 --> 00:13:34.939
and co-workers in Australia because it's
really easy to find in stores it's

00:13:34.939 --> 00:13:40.399
really light and it feels like a nice
moisturiser and it's frequently on sale

00:13:40.399 --> 00:13:44.600
the mecca to save face
super screen SPF 50 plus is quite

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.930
similar in texture but it does tend to
be a little bit pricier my backup

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.649
recommendation is the Coles facial
sunscreen this is a little bit heavier

00:13:51.649 --> 00:13:56.240
but it is really really cheap my final
mention is the Bioderma photoderm

00:13:56.240 --> 00:14:00.230
